      {
        "review_id": 527572449,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r527572449-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A very unique experience!",
        "text": "Being one of the most holy places in Nepal, if you are in Kathmandu you have to go. The place is unlike the other tourist sites in Kathmandu has a very local feel to it. No souvenir shops. A lot of people. you see some tourists but with a lot of with beggars, people who seem to be living there, locals going for worship, locals going for cremation of their deceased with mourning people. It is very unique. I did not explore the whole complex but i just sat there in awe watching how completely different the culture is. I witnessed a couple of cremations from the beginning of washing the bodies' feet in the river to the set up of the cremation site to the actual cremation. It was definitely food for thought. I don't know about the rest of the complex but after an hour just sitting there watching i felt so heavy i needed to leave. Not in a bad way but in a i-need-to-digest-all-this way. I would definitely go again because it is a completely different feel than anywhere else i saw in Nepal. Entrance fee for foreigners is NPR 1,000. Worth at least an hour in my opinion. I did not have a guide.",
