      {
        "review_id": 525927136,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r525927136-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Sit down and take it all in",
        "text": "Great place. It's huge and it quite fascinating to see rituals that are so different than your own. You see the dead having their feet washed, then cremated. It's all very public with an audience. Very different to a western funeral. It is interesting to just sit and watch people interact with each other. Soak it all in because it's amazing what you witness. We saw kids torment the resident crazy lady and then have her murderously run around after them with bamboo sticks. Kids swimming in the god awful coloured river, men coming in singing and dancing while giving an offering to the gods then taking a dip in the river. Amazing stuff.\n\nIf you want a guide, make sure you agree upon a price before you set out. My mistake by not doing that and having to cough up 2000NPR per person just for the guide, ontop of the 1000NPR entry fee for foreigners. My advice, don't take a guide.",
