        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r525395933-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "This gate between live and death is very disturbing",
        "text": "This gate between live and death is very disturbing but a must see as we now know. We went there by coincidence because we gained some time when we took the plane from Pokhara to Kathmandu instead of the bus (saved us 6 hours). To see the public incinerations and the closeness between the different groups of believers, priests, corpses, beggars, monks, apes and tourists is really distressing. The practice of mourning that is so different to the western habits, the burning dead bodies, the smoke the sorrow and the misery...all this is totally different. But this place is the center of Hinduism and very holy. We left it with a deep thoughtfulness.",
